ZEsarPCW -- an Amstrad PCW libretro core
=========================================

Upstream emulator
-----------------
ZEsarUX: Cesar Hernandez Bano and contributors
https://github.com/chernandezba/zesarux
GNU General Public License v3 or later, as stated in the upstream source headers.

ZEsarPCW libretro port
----------------------
retrodiv <retrodiv@proton.me>: libretro port, PCW FDC/uPD765 fidelity work, on-screen keyboard,
floppy sound, per-title gamepad mappings, crop, colour modes, save states and
build tooling, and the native PCW sector bootstrap (GPLv3). The UK/US on-screen-keyboard pixel art, gamepad bindings
and port-authored mapping annotations in `sources/mappings/` are port work under
GPLv3. The initial catalogue identifiers, titles and disc fingerprints derive
from MAME contributors' PCW software list, which carries a CC0-1.0 notice.
The verified reference and maintained additions are recorded in
`licenses/MAPPINGS.md`. The port's changes to the retained ZEsarUX units and its
PCW-specific replacements are recorded in `licenses/MODIFICATIONS.md`.

libretro API
------------
`src/libretro/libretro.h` is the unmodified canonical header pinned to the
RetroArch commit/hash recorded in `licenses/PROVENANCE.md`; its permissive notice
is preserved. Port-authored glue is GPLv3; generated third-party data retains
the terms described below and in `licenses/PROVENANCE.md`.

Embedded data
-------------
The OpenPCW-OS helper disk (https://github.com/retrodiv/OpenPCW-OS)
is built from retrodiv <retrodiv@proton.me>'s original MIT-licensed sources. Its display
face uses Microsoft's MIT-licensed MS-DOS 4.0 CP437 8x8 source; the exact source,
notice, commit, transformations and hashes are recorded in the same provenance
document.
The complete upstream distribution notices are preserved in
`sources/openpcw-os/LICENSES.txt` and accompany the embedded disk.
The floppy PCM data and its exact WAV source in `sources/fdc/` derive from
PituKa/wiituka by David Colmenero (D_Skywalk), GPLv2-or-later, distributed here
using GPLv3. The pinned source headers preserve his copyright and licence
notice; the extracted WAV sources and regeneration tool are bundled in
`sources/fdc/`. Exact provenance, hashes and transformations are recorded in
`licenses/PROVENANCE.md`.
